From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:39:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] phy: samsung-ufs: Add Exynos9820 support

The M-PHY of this SoC is taken through the same four points as the ones
already here, with the calibration values of the vendor kernel for it.
Each line of the tables names the line it was taken from.

Two things differ from what the driver does by default, and the driver
data says so rather than the tables working around it.  The calibration
this PHY reports on is set going by the table written after the link is
up, not by the first one, so its wait belongs at that later point.  And
the receiver has to be locked onto the incoming data before the last
table is written rather than after it, so that wait comes first; each
miss takes the clock recovery block of the lane down and back up, which
is what the vendor does, and after a hundred tries it gives up.

The two lanes sit a quarter of the register window apart rather than at
the usual spacing, and one register takes a different value in the first
gear than in every gear above it.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
